# KATAPP-SPLIT1 (owner 2026-10-19) — which Worker this repo deploys as. build-static.sh refuses
# to build without this file, so nothing from katapp can deploy as plain "katui" (labs, which
# stays on phpjabbers as the benchmark until the owner rewires it).
#   KATUI_NAME     the Worker's name — must match the Cloudflare Worker git-connected to this repo
#   KATUI_DOMAIN   its custom domain (wrangler attaches it on deploy)
#   PAGES_SERVICE  the Worker that serves /keaton, /deal and /legacy (they stayed in phpjabbers);
#                  must never be KATUI_NAME itself. When labs moves here, this becomes a Worker
#                  built from phpjabbers for those pages alone.
KATUI_NAME=katui-lab1
KATUI_DOMAIN=lab1.katomia.com
PAGES_SERVICE=katui
# LABS-PROMOTE1 (owner 2026-11-10: "lab1 should become the status quo … labs.katomia.com is our
# pseudo-production … let lab1 evolve whilst leaving labs at a particular commit"). The SAME build
# also gets a second Worker config, build/dist/wrangler.labs.toml, for the Worker that serves labs.
# That Worker is git-connected to branch `labs`; promoting = `git push origin <commit>:labs` (a
# fast-forward to a commit already proven on lab1). Only the Worker name and domain differ.
LABS_NAME=katui-labs
# APP-DOMAIN1 (owner 2026-11-10): app.katomia.com serves the same Worker as labs for now (the
# domain HashPack will be asked to approve). Space-separated; every domain the labs Worker should
# keep must be listed (a deploy detaches any it does not name). To split app off later, give it
# its own Worker and branch and take it out of this list.
LABS_DOMAINS="labs.katomia.com app.katomia.com"
